menu "AI-Gauge updates"

    config AI_GAUGE_UPDATE_REPO
        string "GitHub repository that publishes firmware releases"
        default "JosephGarrone/ai-gauge"
        help
            owner/name of the repository whose latest release the gauge updates from. The release
            must carry ota.json and ai-gauge.bin, which release.yml attaches (docs/ci-release.md).
            A fork that publishes its own releases changes this.

    config AI_GAUGE_UPDATE_AUTO_CHECK
        bool "Check for updates automatically while on WiFi"
        default y
        help
            Look for a newer release a minute after connecting, then twice a day. Only checks:
            installing always takes a confirmed tap on the settings page or POST /api/update/install,
            because an install restarts the gauge.

endmenu
